From e59a89b26486eaf95ccebce34d55398fa3cb4b29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/41] network radio: Find NAS - the Tab5 asks the network for
 the relay's address

Relay: answers a UDP "QMXR?" on port 7355 (same number as the TCP service)
with "QMXR! <its IP> <TCP port>", picking the address of the interface that
reaches the asker. Nothing is sent unless asked. --discovery-port N / 0.
nettest.py checks it by unicast (required) and broadcast (informational).

Tab5: radio_relay_discover() broadcasts QMXR? three times over 1.5 s and
collects distinct answers. The Radio source panel has a Find NAS button;
the search runs on a short-lived task (never the LVGL task) and fills in
the first address found, listing any others.

Tested: relay with --fake (nettest PASSED incl. discovery; junk ignored);
radio_relay_discover() compiled on Linux against the real relay - broadcast
found it, no listener gives 0 after 1.5 s, duplicate answers merged, WiFi
down gives -1. ui.c and radio_relay.c compile with the Tab5 build flags.

